Pagination --- the process of dividing a large amount of content or data into smaller, discrete, numbered pages or sections ... ... so PAGE is RESULT of query .. OPTIMIZE output .. and ther SEO best practices for WEb pages 
the process of dividing a large set of digital data, content, or application records into smaller, distinct segments or "pages"

Make sure the API query includes both the pageInfo parameter and a first variable (where 0 < first ≤ 10,000) that determines the batch size of each iteration.
Pagination ..quick search returns only 50 requests but 
The hasNextPage attribute indicates whether there are more pages to load, and you receive the next page endCursor as long as there is a next page. To receive these attributes in the response, you must explicitly tell the API that you want the pageInfo response node to populate in the responses.
To paginate your results:

Run a query to get results. Make sure pageInfo is in the request.
If hasNextPage response parameter exists in pageInfo, then:
a. Run the query again starting from endCursor.
b. Save new pageInfo.
c. Repeat.
Make sure the API query includes both the pageInfo parameter and a first variable (where 0 < first ≤ 10,000) that determines the batch size of each iteration.
